# msgpack (GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964) and setuptools (CVE-2025-47273) are flagged by Trivy
# at versions 1.1.2 / 70.3.0, but those versions come from pip's own internal
# vendor.txt manifest (/usr/local/.../site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt), which
# just records which versions pip vendors for its own bundled/internal use. This is
# not an installed application package and is not reachable via this connector's
# code or any untrusted external input.
#
# The actual application-facing msgpack/setuptools packages installed in the venv
# resolve to current, non-vulnerable versions via normal pip install (no explicit
# pin needed in requirements.txt). Verified 2026-09-15 in the built image:
#   pip show msgpack     -> 1.2.2
#   pip show setuptools  -> 84.0.0
#
# Re-evaluate if pip itself bumps its vendored copies to fixed versions, or if a
# future finding shows a real installed-package occurrence (not pip/_vendor).
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
